WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:15.762
Unit thirty-one: Passive Voice (is made / was built). Today you will focus on the action instead of the person who did it.

4
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:18.842
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.033
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:24.699
Passive.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:29.192
Passive means a verb form where the subject receives the action.

8
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.400
The passive is used here.

9
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:34.670
Your turn. Say: Passive.

10
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:38.395
Passive.

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.256
Is made.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.888
Is made means the passive of make in the present.

13
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:45.902
Rice is made here.

14
00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:48.914
Your turn. Say: Is made.

15
00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:52.698
Is made.

16
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.242
Are made.

17
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.144
Are made means the plural passive of make in the present.

18
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.390
Shoes are made in a factory.

19
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:03.311
Your turn. Say: Are made.

20
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.226
Are made.

21
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:08.961
Was built.

22
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.658
Was built means the passive of build in the past.

23
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.191
The temple was built long ago.

24
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.076
Your turn. Say: Was built.

25
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:21.981
Was built.

26
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:23.671
Were built.

27
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:27.449
Were built means the plural passive of build in the past.

28
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:31.071
These houses were built in 1990.

29
00:01:31.683 --> 00:01:34.312
Your turn. Say: Were built.

30
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.388
Were built.

31
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:39.965
By.

32
00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.240
By means used to show who did the action.

33
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.292
The book was written by her.

34
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:48.756
Your turn. Say: By.

35
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.450
By.

36
00:01:53.217 --> 00:01:54.078
Object.

37
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:57.512
Object means the thing that receives the action.

38
00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.443
The ball is the object.

39
00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.459
Your turn. Say: Object.

40
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.301
Object.

41
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:07.958
Agent.

42
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.356
Agent means the person who does the action.

43
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.450
The agent is the writer.

44
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.470
Your turn. Say: Agent.

45
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:20.242
Agent.

46
00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:24.371
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:28.461
Visal, who built Angkor Wat? Do we know the person?

48
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:38.788
Angkor Wat was built a long time ago. The passive is useful when the action is more important than the person. Form: be + past participle.

49
00:02:39.883 --> 00:02:42.080
How do we change an active sentence?

50
00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:55.150
Active: Workers make shoes here. Passive: Shoes are made here. The object becomes the subject, be changes to match it, and the verb becomes the past participle.

51
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.669
When do we use by?

52
00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:11.632
Only if the agent is important: The song was written by a famous singer. If it is not important, leave it out. Use am, is or are for the present and was or were for the past.

53
00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.499
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.381
Grammar focus: Passive: be plus past participle.

55
00:03:19.681 --> 00:03:20.810
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.517 --> 00:03:23.481
Rice is grown in Cambodia.

57
00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:26.522
The temple was built a long time ago.

58
00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:29.637
The song was written by a famous singer.

59
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.505
Form the passive with am / is / are / was / were + past participle. Use by only when the agent is important.

60
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.121
Be careful! Don't say: The letter was wrote by her.

61
00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.670
Say: The letter was written by her.

62
00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.737
Use the past participle.

63
00:03:47.533 --> 00:03:50.093
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.982
Things Are Made.

65
00:03:52.282 --> 00:03:54.804
Rice is grown in many parts of Cambodia.

66
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.974
This temple was built a long time ago.

67
00:03:58.967 --> 00:04:00.897
These shoes were made in a factory.

68
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.109
The song was written by a famous singer.

69
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.564
Many things around us are made by machines.

70
00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:12.680
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.517 --> 00:04:15.389
Rice blank in Cambodia.

72
00:04:15.689 --> 00:04:19.110
A, grows. B, is grown. C, grown.

73
00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.782
The answer is B: is grown.

74
00:04:25.917 --> 00:04:28.706
The house blank in 1990.

75
00:04:29.006 --> 00:04:32.427
A, was built. B, is built. C, built.

76
00:04:35.967 --> 00:04:37.595
The answer is A: was built.

77
00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.599
These shoes blank in a factory.

78
00:04:40.899 --> 00:04:44.482
A, was made. B, are made. C, make.

79
00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.801
The answer is B: are made.

80
00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.659
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:58.853
A, The letter wrote by her.. B, The letter was written by her.. C, The letter was wrote by her..

82
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.934
The answer is B: The letter was written by her..

83
00:05:06.083 --> 00:05:08.512
According to the reading, who wrote the song?

84
00:05:08.812 --> 00:05:13.290
A, a famous singer. B, a machine. C, a farmer.

85
00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.053
The answer is A: a famous singer.

86
00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:23.232
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:27.244
Write one sentence about something that is made or was built.

88
00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.620
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:51.303
Many bridges in my city were built in the last ten years. Rice is grown near my village. In these sentences I use the passive, because the action is more important than the person who did it.

90
00:05:51.603 --> 00:05:53.312
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.217 --> 00:05:59.830
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive: be plus past participle.

92
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:05.150
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

93
00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:08.068
See you in Unit thirty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:12.309
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

